\section{Cloudflare R2}{
You need three things, all from the Cloudflare dashboard:
\enumerate{
\item \strong{Account ID}: R2 overview page, right-hand \emph{Account Details} panel.
\item \strong{Access key + secret key}: \emph{Manage R2 API Tokens} > \emph{Create API
Token} with "Object Read & Write" permission. The token-creation
screen shows the Access Key ID and Secret Access Key once -- store
them (e.g. in \verb{~/.Renviron}).
\item \strong{Bucket name}: the name you gave the bucket when creating it.
}

R2's S3 API requires \code{region=auto}; the helper sets this for you.
}

\section{Amazon S3}{
Credentials follow the standard AWS chain: \code{AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID} /
\code{AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY} environment variables, shared config files
(\verb{~/.aws/credentials}), or an attached IAM role. Supply \code{access_key} /
\code{secret_key} only if you want to override that chain for this command.
}

\section{Google Cloud Storage}{
Authentication uses Application Default Credentials. Either run
\verb{gcloud auth application-default login} once, or create a service account
key (IAM & Admin > Service Accounts > Keys) and pass its JSON file path
as \code{credentials_file}.
}

\section{Azure Blob Storage}{
Find the storage account's access keys under \emph{Storage account} >
\emph{Security + networking} > \emph{Access keys} in the Azure portal. Pass one as
\code{access_key}, or use a SAS token via \code{sas_token}. If neither is given,
the \code{AZURE_STORAGE_KEY} / \code{AZURE_STORAGE_SAS_TOKEN} environment variables
are used.
}

\section{Other S3-compatible services}{
Use \code{s3_compatible_bucket()} with the provider's endpoint:\tabular{lll}{
   Provider \tab Endpoint \tab Notes \cr
   MinIO \tab \verb{https://minio.example.com} \tab needs \code{path_style = TRUE} and \code{region} \cr
   DigitalOcean Spaces \tab \verb{https://\{region\}.digitaloceanspaces.com} \tab region inferred \cr
   Backblaze B2 \tab \verb{https://s3.\{region\}.backblazeb2.com} \tab region inferred \cr
   Source Cooperative \tab \verb{https://data.source.coop} \tab bucket is your org name; pass \code{session_token} \cr
}
}

